.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MAIL 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mail
.Nd local mbox and Maildir mail reader and sender
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar mailbox
.Op Fl s Ar subject
.Op Fl b Ar body-file
.Ar recipient ...
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar mailbox
.Op Fl H | e | r Ar N | d Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and writes one local mbox file or Maildir.
With recipients it appends a message to the selected store; the body comes from standard input
or from
.Fl b Ar body-file .
With no action it lists message headers.
The supported actions are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl H
List headers explicitly.
.It Fl e
Exit 0 when at least one message exists, 1 otherwise.
.It Fl r Ar N
Read message
.Ar N
(one-based).
.It Fl d Ar N
Delete message
.Ar N .
.El
.Pp
The store is selected by
.Fl f ,
then the
.Ev MAIL
environment variable, then
.Pa $HOME/Maildir ,
.Pa $HOME/.maildir
or
.Pa $HOME/mbox .
A directory is treated as a Maildir; a regular file is treated as mbox.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar subject
Subject for an outgoing message.
.It Fl b Ar body-file
Read the body from
.Ar body-file ;
.Li -
means standard input.
.It Fl f Ar mailbox
Select the mbox file or Maildir.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MAIL
.It Ev MAIL
Default mailbox when
.Fl f
is absent.
.It Ev USER , LOGNAME
Sender name used in the local
.Li From:
header.
.It Ev HOME
Base for the default Maildir/mbox selection.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width $HOME/Maildir
.It Pa $HOME/Maildir
Preferred default Maildir.
.It Pa $HOME/mbox
Fallback mbox.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error or an unsupported option exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mailx 1
.Sh BUGS
Reply, forward, SMTP/network delivery, cc/bcc, attachments and an interactive prompt are not
implemented.
